+# G3 literal source scan - PROPOSED two-tier scope (NOT APPROVED, NOT ACTIVE)
+
+Status: proposal only. review/arbitration.md records that no vendor exception
+was approved. Applying this requires an explicit owner/S16 ruling.
+
+Tier A (release-blocking, unchanged strictness): scan all first-party sources
+  under the whole tree, excluding only generated outputs and straw-app/third-party/.
+Tier B (provenance, still enforced): straw-app/third-party/ is NOT skipped silently.
+  It must (1) contain NOTICE.md, (2) have svelte/LICENSE.md and clsx/LICENSE,
+  (3) match the pinned versions in NOTICE.md, (4) have its matches enumerated
+  in the evidence log (count and file list), never hidden or renamed.
+Upstream identifiers stay byte-for-byte; nothing is disguised to pass.
+Current observed result (STRAW-001-VERIFICATION.md): 95 upstream matches,
+  0 first-party matches. G3 remains FAIL until a ruling is recorded.
